 r←gridCellSet values
⍝ A Grid's CellSet is DERIVED from Values, not stored independently of it.
⍝ Measured against native Dyalog 20.0 (Win32 Grid) - see tests/test_gridShadowProps:
⍝   - ⎕WG'CellSet' always reports ⍴Values, from ⎕WC onwards, even if never set.
⍝   - every ⎕WS'Values' REGENERATES it as (⍴Values)⍴1: a CellSet the app had
⍝     previously set to 0s does not survive the next Values write.
⍝   - it is 1 for every cell regardless of content - '' and ⍬ cells still read 1.
⍝     It means "this cell exists", not "this cell holds something".
⍝   - an explicitly supplied CellSet beats this, in either order, in both ⎕WC and
⍝     ⎕WS, so callers must apply it only when CellSet is absent from the call.
⍝
⍝ EWC keeps properties as independent arrays in the server-side namespace, so
⍝ without this CellSet sits at its 0 0 class default while Values grows. Apps
⍝ doing array maths across the pair then break - GAMA's GridConfigure does
⍝ M←M⍪(⍴z)⍴0 to extend CellSet alongside Values and gets a LENGTH ERROR.
⍝
⍝ Note CellTypes is NOT like this: native never reshapes it on a Values write.
⍝ See fixSendEvents for how that mismatch is absorbed instead.
 r←(⍴values)⍴1
